 derived from strategic company objectives</li><li>Integrate Walaris software and technology into military and security systems to add autonomous capabilities and boost overall system performance</li><li>Develop software solutions that improve system reliability, deployment velocity, and developer experience </li><li>Own and deliver complex features end-to-end across the full stack, from web-based frontend interfaces through distributed backend services and technical design through production deployment iteration</li><li>Ensure compliance with relevant military safety and quality standards</li><li>Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure that requirements from R&amp;D, sales, and product management are fully integrated and effectively addressed throughout the development process</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Bachelor's or master's degree in computer science, software engineering, electrical engineering, information technology, or a comparable qualification </li><li>Professional experience in the development of complex software systems with strong proficiency in Rust, C++, or Python</li><li>Experience with distributed systems and system integration</li><li>Hands-on experience with multithreading and concurrency, asynchronous and distributed systems, containerized architectures (e.g., Docker-based environments), messaging systems (e.g., ZeroMQ, DDS, NATS, or similar), and performance optimization and system tuning </li><li>Expertise in software development on Linux platforms </li></ul><ul><li>Solid understanding of networking protocols and communication mechanisms, including TCP/IP, UDP, and inter-process communication (IPC) </li></ul><ul><li>Experience designing and working with REST APIs </li></ul><ul><li>Knowledge of low-latency communication systems</li></ul><ul><li>Fluent in English and German </li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Preferred Qualifications </strong></p><ul><li>Experience with high-availability and fault-tolerant systems </li><li>Understanding of real-time and deterministic system requirements </li><li>Experience with sensor integration and multi-modal sensor fusion in event-driven systems</li><li>Background in geospatial data systems (GIS/geoinformatics) or processing of time-series data </li></ul><ul><li>Experience building software according to DALs and standards like DO-278, DO-178, or ASIL</li></ul><ul><li>Familiarity with NATO standards like SAPIENT, STANAG 4586, etc.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p>Join our mission and become part of an innovative, dynamic team! At Walaris, you’ll play a vital role in saving lives and safeguarding local and national security by harnessing the power of cutting-edge technologies. This is your chance to break new ground and take on meaningful responsibility as you help develop and deploy industry-defining solutions.</p><p>We offer creative freedom, competitive compensation, and a fast-paced, collaborative environment where your ideas and contributions truly matter.</p><p>If you’re ready to make an impact, we invite you to apply by submitting your cover letter, resume, and transcript through our online application form.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/walaris/c2-software-engineer-nuremberg-408085","tags":["Engineering","Information Technology and Services","Software Development"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Nuremberg, Germany","created_at":1790799615},{"slug":"embedded-software-engineer-adam-audio-gmbh-berlin-95425","company_name":"Focusrite","title":"Embedded Software Engineer (m/f/d) - ADAM Audio GmbH","description":"<p><strong>Embedded Software Engineer (m/f/d) – ADAM Audio GmbH</strong></p><p><strong>Location: </strong>Berlin offices / hybrid</p><p><strong>Term: </strong>Full-time, permanent</p><p><strong>Salary:</strong> Depending on experience</p><p>Start date: as soon as possible</p><ul><li>Are you passionate about engineering and its application to acoustics and audio reproduction?</li><li>Are you an Embedded Software Engineer looking to join an innovative team for creating audio products?</li></ul><p>If the answer to these questions is yes, then we’d love to hear from you!</p><p>At ADAM Audio, our profound passion for audio and acoustics drives our pursuit for excellence. We are pushing the boundaries of innovation in the field of audio and acoustics. Our commitment to excellence and cutting-edge engineering drives our mission to deliver ground-breaking solutions to our customers. The successful candidate with have previous experience in audio electronics.</p><p><strong>Your Role and Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li>You will be collaborating closely with cross-functional and multi-cultural teams across the company and external partners, to define, prototype and develop products from early sketches on to market introduction and maintenance.</li></ul><ul><li>On a day-to-day basis you’ll be responsible for providing the firmware code for our hardware products, including evaluation of new technologies, debugging prototype hardware and ensuring your code is suitable for mass production and complies with latest market regulations (CE, FCC, CRA etc.). You'll have the opportunity to shape the direction of our embedded projects and you’ll be involved in the project's lifecycles. You’ll be refining product specifications, producing innovative designs and solutions and engaging with a multi-discipline team. You’ll be planning your activities, estimating your work and collaborating to meet deadlines and product requirements as well as working hands-on at functional prototypes and evaluation boards to debug and test electronic hardware designs with your code on it.</li></ul><ul><li>Individual and team development is important, and we’ll support you as you look for ways to grow and improve your personal knowledge and skills. We’ll also be looking for you to own and help improve our approach to embedded software engineering, including best practices, processes, and tools. There will also be opportunities to share knowledge and practices with all companies across the Focusrite group.</li></ul><p><strong>Skills and Experience Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Expert experience with micro-controllers and audio DSP (Digital Signal Processing) in general</li><li>Mastery in low-level programming at ARM-based-microcontrollers (STM32, NXP, etc.) and RTOS</li><li>Experience in C and modern C++ programming and common frameworks like Zephyr</li><li>Experience in working at systems with hard real-time constraints</li><li>Mastering a range of test equipment: oscilloscopes, logic analysers, bus analysers and audio analysers (Audio Precision)</li><li>Experience with meeting compliance regulations and standards (CE, FCC, EMC, RED, LVD etc.) for USB-, wireless- and Ethernet-connectivity, and battery powered devices</li><li>Experience with common Bluetooth and RF SoCs like Qualcomm, Airoha, Bestec etc.</li><li>Experience with networking protocols and chips/modules for Ethernet, WiFi and BLE</li><li>Strong ability to analyse and present trade-offs between cost, quality, and development time</li><li>Hands-on problem-solving and debugging skills, including lab work (test equipment, soldering etc.)</li><li>Excellent communication skills and ability to collaborate effectively with multi-disciplinary teams</li><li>Good English language skills (spoken and written) and ideally good German language skills.</li></ul><p><strong>Beneficial:</strong></p><ul><li>A Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Information Technology, Electronics Engineering (or other relevant technical disciplines)</li><li>Familiarity with electronics and/or audio engineering.</li></ul><p><strong>What can you expect from us?</strong></p><p>Well, our colleagues are fantastic, of course! Here are some more good reasons to join our team:</p><ul><li>Flexible working hours for a better work-life balance</li><li>A healthy mix of remote and office work</li><li>A harmonious and appreciative working atmosphere</li><li>Work on exciting projects in a unique industry as part of an international brand group</li><li>Employee discounts, including on Focusrite, Novation and Sequential products</li><li>Opportunities for professional development</li><li>ADAM Audio bonus programme – our employees share in the company's joint success!</li><li>Company pension scheme, ADAM Audio health programme, mental health first aiders, FeelGood Manager, Business Bike programme, regular staff events and much more.</li></ul><p><strong>You don’t have all the experience we’ve asked for?</strong></p><p>Our priority is to find the right fit for the team and for the company, and we will always do what we can to support your individual development. In other words, if you don’t quite have all the experience listed above, we’d still be interested in hearing from you. Let us know what you would bring to the role, and why you’d be a great fit for the team.</p><p>We look forward to receiving your application!</p><p><strong>About us</strong></p><p>ADAM Audio GmbH is a rapidly growing, internationally positioned Focusrite plc company based in Berlin Adlershof.</p><p>We are one of the market-leading manufacturers of professional monitoring solutions. &nbsp;</p><p>Our customers include renowned recording studios and well-known music producers all over the world, and our products have also been used to soundtrack numerous Oscar-nominated films in recent years.</p><p>Since 2019, ADAM Audio has been part of Focusrite plc which houses other, highly respected pro audio brands like Martin Audio, Optimal Audio, Sequential, Focusrite, Focusrite Pro, Novation and Ampify. Our international team at the Berlin-based HQ and the office in China live our passion for music. We constantly drive ourselves to bring fresh ideas and new technologies to our high-quality products to meet the needs of pro audio enthusiasts and recording professionals alike.</p><p>We pride ourselves in providing some of the tools that empower creatives all over the world to bring their visions to life. Covering a wide range of products for different levels and budgets, we engage with artists, producers and engineers to become a companion throughout the various stages of their journey.</p><p>Our whole business is structured to let everyone contribute and be heard at all levels, and we make sure it’s a great place to work. As a team, we work hard and support each other to master our individual tasks, building and developing the skills of talented and passionate people – to achieve a common goal. So, if you think you can bring something new to the mix, we look forward to hearing from you.</p><p>ADAM Audio is an equal opportunity employer. Our employees span a wide range of diverse backgrounds, and we believe that embracing diversity is one of the keys to our future success.</p><p>If you want to learn more about the ADAM Audio brand, please go to <a href="https://www.adam-audio.com" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external">www.adam-audio.com</a></p><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/focusrite/embedded-software-engineer-adam-audio-gmbh-berlin-95425","tags":["Engineering","Music","ADAM Audio"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Berlin, Germany","created_at":1790799603},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-wealth-ai-berlin-387564","company_name":"Getquin","title":"Senior Product Manager, Wealth & AI (f/m/d)","description":"<br><strong>What we do</strong><p><p>At getquin, we're on a mission to empower everyone to build wealth.</p><p>Founded in 2020, we started with a simple idea: help people see their entire financial life in one place, so they can make more informed decisions.</p><p>Today, getquin has grown into one of the largest wealth platforms globally, already helping over half a million users manage and grow their wealth. Our platform combines analytics, tools and community to make wealth-building accessible for everyone, not just the experts.</p><p>After launching in Germany, we've started expanding across Europe, with a focus on growing our user base, building valuable new features and helping even more people take control of their financial future.</p><p>If you're excited to help shape the future of personal wealth management, join us. We're just getting started.</p></p><br><strong>What you'll be doing</strong><p><p>You've built products for investors. You know what a TER actually does to a long-run return, why a user with four brokers has no visbility what they really own, and how differently people behave when the number on screen is their pension rather than their pocket money.</p><p>You've probably also hit the ceiling of what a chart can tell someone. Better tables, more filters, another allocation donut. The data was always there; the answer never quite arrived.</p><p>We have something nobody else has: a complete, cross-institution picture of a person's wealth. Investments, cash, liabilities and insurance contracts, in one place, for over half a million users. Your work is turning that into features and insights people understand and act on, and the interesting tools for doing that now include AI.</p><p>We're looking for an experienced Senior Product Manager to own that area. You'll work directly with the founders and the product team, alongside engineering and our financial advisory teams. This is a senior individual contributor role with no direct reports, and you'll mentor less experienced product managers on the team.</p><p><strong>Own the wealth product area end to end</strong></p><ul><li>Set the product strategy and roadmap across the picture we give people of their wealth and how we help them optimize it</li><li>Decide what we build on aggregated portfolio data that nobody with a single-broker view could build at all</li><li>Own our efforts to stay on the forefront of digital wealth management services and play your part in disrupting a still very offline industry</li><li>Work the unglamorous, high-leverage problems too: data quality, coverage gaps, missing cost basis, duplicate holdings across connections, ETFs held through more than one broker. A portfolio insight is only as trustworthy as the numbers under it</li></ul><p><strong>Turn the data into something users act on</strong></p><ul><li>Define the insights we surface about someone's portfolio, cash position and risk, and why each one earns a place on their screen</li><li>Own our conversational AI assistant and our AI-driven insights: what they say, what they refuse to say, and how a user knows which is which</li><li>Set the quality bar for anything we tell a user about their money: accuracy targets, human review, guardrails, rollback. Decide when something is good enough to ship and hold that line when the pressure is to ship anyway</li></ul><p><strong>Own the numbers</strong></p><ul><li>Define the metrics for your area: activation, engagement, the insight-to-action funnel, and contribution to subscription conversion and retention</li><li>Run the experiments, including proper A/B testing, read them, and report what didn't work alongside what did</li><li>Live in your own product analytics and write your own queries and reporting, rather than wait for someone to give that to you</li></ul></p><br><strong>What we are looking for</strong><p><p><strong>You might be a fit if:</strong></p><ul><li>You've built wealth management, investing or portfolio products. You know the domain properly: instruments, ETFs, costs, allocation, risk, tax drag, and how retail investors actually behave rather than how they should. This is the requirement we're least flexible on</li><li>You've owned a product area end to end against a number you defined yourself, with real experimentation behind it</li><li>You've shipped at least one AI or LLM-based feature to production for real users, and you owned its output quality. </li><li>You've shipped inside a legal or compliance constraint, and you can reason about where an insight becomes advice. </li><li>Your product discovery produces evidence, not opinion. You can show us a real research artefact and a decision that changed because of it</li><li>You're fluent in English; German is a plus</li><li>You can work from our Berlin office, and you already have the right to work in Germany</li></ul><p>That usually adds up to around five or more years in product, but we care about the evidence, not the year count. If you came to product from engineering, data science, research, design, financial services, or from a Product Owner role, that counts. </p><p><strong>Strong plus if you have:</strong></p><ul><li>PSD2, open banking or account aggregation experience</li><li>Insurance or brokerage product exposure, which matters as we move into advisory</li><li>Recommendation systems or personalisation at scale</li><li>Subscription and paywall experimentation</li><li>Experience mentoring or coaching other product managers</li><li>Your own portfolio, and opinions about it</li></ul><p>If you meet most of this and not all of it, apply. We'd rather read your application than guess.</p><p><strong>Work authorisation</strong></p><p><strong>This role requires an existing right to work in Germany.</strong> We're not able to sponsor visas or support relocation for this position, so we can only consider candidates who already hold German or EU work authorisation, or who can obtain it independently. We'd rather tell you now than after four conversations.</p><p><strong>What the first six months look like</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Month 1:</strong> you know the data model, the aggregation layer and its technology behind it. What our analytics do and don't cover, and understand how AI is already being used and where it. You've written down the three things you think are most wrong with the product today</li><li><strong>Months 2 to 3:</strong> a written, agreed area strategy with a prioritised roadmap, a primary metric with a baseline, and, clear metrics that you will be monitoring and optimizing along the way</li><li><strong>Months 3 to 4:</strong> the first thing you scoped is live to a user segment, with a read on the primary metric, and with quality measurement behind it if it involves generated output</li><li><strong>Months 5 to 6:</strong> two or three shipped iterations with measured results, including the ones that didn't work, a quality bar the team applies without you in the room, and at least one junior product manager who's visibly better at their job because of you</li></ul><p>You won't be measured on shipping volume. You'll be measured on whether your area got measurably more useful and more trustworthy.</p></p><br><strong>Why join getquin?</strong><p><p><strong>Why join getquin?</strong></p><p>We're a fast-growing B2C fintech, and here, your work has real impact. From day one, you'll take ownership of your domain, ship features end-to-end, and help shape the direction of a product used across Europe. We value initiative, ownership and creativity, not layers of process.</p><p>Three things that are specifically true of this role:</p><ul><li><strong>Wealth management is ripe for disruption. </strong>Following digitalisation waves of banking and brokerage services, we are leading those efforts across the next big topic for private individuals: better understand  and optimize your wealth</li><li><strong>The data asset is genuinely rare.</strong> Aggregated cross-institution wealth for half a million people, with over +€25bn in connected assets. Trade Republic sees its own platform. N26 sees the current account. Nobody else in Europe sees the whole picture, which means there are product questions you can only answer here</li><li><strong>You'll own the area, not a slice of it.</strong> At our size the decisions are yours</li></ul><p>Ready to build something meaningful? Then join us at the forefront of making wealth building accessible to everyone.</p><p><strong>How we hire</strong></p><p>Five conversations, typically three to four weeks from first call to decision. We tell you where you stand after every step, and we respond within seven days at every stage.</p><ol><li><strong>Recruiter screen, 30 min, video.</strong> Role, scope, the salary band, hybrid expectation, notice period, work authorisation. No trick questions</li><li><strong>Hiring manager, 60 min, video.</strong> Your product area ownership, the outcome you drove, and your depth in the wealth domain. This is the first real fit conversation, in both directions</li><li><strong>Product case, take home.</strong> We give you a real getquin problem on aggregated wealth data and work through it together. We know you already have a job, hence we do not impose an in-person case during working hours</li><li><strong>Cross-functional panel, 2 x 30 min, in our Berlin office.</strong> Cover in more depth your case study and deep dive further in your understanding of product metrics and approach to product development. Usually in person in our office.</li><li><strong>Close conversation, 30 min.</strong> Team fit, how you like to work, and whatever is still open, including your questions for a founder</li></ol><p>Along the last part we will be making reference checks, but only with former employers. Once we have this, we will make you a formal offer. </p><p>The whole loop runs in English. Tell us if you need any adjustment to the process, whether timing, format or accessibility, and we'll make it. You don't need to explain why.</p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/getquin/senior-product-manager-wealth-ai-berlin-387564","tags":["Product Management","Product Strategy","Senior Product Manager","Product Lead","Wealth M