enet-group/praktikant-all-genders-3-6-monate-im-creative-content-team-munchen-467611","tags":["Bezahlte Praktikumstellen München","Praktikum Stelle in München im Bereich Marketing","Offene Praktikanten Stellen in München","Praktikum Consumer Promotions München Vollzeit","Vollzeitpraktikum Kampagnenmanagement München","Bezahltes Praktikum Produktmanagement"],"job_types":["Entry","Intern","Full time"],"location":"München","created_at":1790798956},{"slug":"product-engineer-backend-ai-at-briink-berlin-497158","company_name":"Merantix","title":"Product Engineer (Backend/AI) @Briink","description":"<br><strong>What we do</strong><p>At <strong>Briink</strong>, we’re building AI technology for the global sustainability economy. We work with the world’s largest climate organizations, including CDP and PRI, and multinational companies such as Bayer, Siemens, Commerzbank, E.ON, and Heidelberg Materials.<br><br>Our technology helps automate how sustainability data is collected, analyzed, verified, and acted on. Through our work with global climate organizations, what you build at Briink will directly impact the sustainability workflows of more than 30,000 companies, investors, and cities worldwide.<br><br>We’re a small team working at enormous scale. Your code won’t sit behind an internal tool or an experimental demo — it will help shape how some of the world’s largest organizations understand and act on their environmental impact. Based at Berlin’s AI Campus, with a second office in London, and backed by over €7 million in funding, we want to prove that some of the world’s most powerful technology can also be a powerful force for good.<br><br>Application requirement: Intro video<br>As part of your application, please submit a short <strong>intro video (max 2 minutes)</strong> answering:<br><ol><li>Who you are and what you have done/built that is relevant for this role. </li><li>Why you’re excited about owning and shipping AI-powered products at Briink. </li><li>Why Briink’s sustainability mission resonates with you.</li></ol>Upload your video using this <a href="https://forms.gle/YSy4HPV5QQg5hFCx6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">form</a> (YouTube unlisted, Loom, or any other solution is fine). We do this to get a better sense of candidates before continuing the process. Any application without a video will not be considered ;)</p><br><strong>Your role</strong><p>As Briink’s <strong>Backend/AI Product Engineer</strong>, you’ll join a small, high-ownership product and engineering team building AI-powered products for sustainability professionals.<br><br>This is not a narrowly scoped backend role. You’ll take meaningful product problems from initial discovery and user conversations through technical design, implementation, and iteration to deploy them at scale across the ESG market. You’ll combine strong backend and AI/LLM engineering with product judgement and the initiative to work out what should be built - not just how to action a predefined ticket.<br><br>You will:<br><ul><li><strong>Own product features end to end</strong>, from understanding the user problem and defining the right approach through to delivery, measurement, and improvement.</li><li><strong>Design and build scalable backend systems</strong>, including APIs, data models, workflows, and infrastructure for complex enterprise products.</li><li><strong>Build and ship applied AI/LLM features</strong>, such as LLM chains, RAG systems, tool-using agents, structured-output pipelines, and evaluation workflows</li><li><strong>Create reusable, extensible platform building blocks</strong> that support multiple user journeys and reporting workflows rather than solving each problem in isolation.</li><li><strong>Improve the robustness of our systems</strong>, strengthening reliability, testing, observability, performance, and maintainability as we scale.</li><li><strong>Work directly with users, product, and data</strong>, using qualitative feedback and product data to understand the real problem and evaluate whether a solution works.</li><li><strong>Prototype and test new AI capabilities</strong>, turning promising ideas into practical product improvements that accelerate our roadmap.</li><li><strong>Bring thoughtful opinions and constructive challenge</strong>, helping the team make better product and technical decisions.</li><li><strong>Collaborate closely with other engineers</strong>, including through pair programming, technical design discussions, and shared problem-solving.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p>Technical requirements<ul><li><strong>Strong professional backend engineering experience</strong>, with a track record of designing and shipping reliable production systems.</li><li><strong>Experience in a small, high-ownership product team</strong>, ideally within a startup or scale-up engineering organisation of roughly 5–20 engineers.</li><li><strong>Evidence that you have shipped meaningful products end to end</strong>, rather than owning only a narrow component within a much larger organisation.</li><li><strong>Strong experience in Python</strong> (or another modern backend language such as Java, Ruby, or TypeScript, combined with the ability and willingness to become productive in Python quickly).</li><li><strong>Strong API, database, and systems design skills</strong>, with the ability to model complex workflows and build maintainable foundations for enterprise products.</li><li><strong>Applied AI/LLM experience</strong>: you have experience or a strong interest in LLM-powered features, ideally involving RAG or retrieval, tool use, agents, structured outputs, or evaluation systems.</li><li><strong>A solid software-quality mindset</strong>, including testing, code review, CI/CD, observability, and pragmatic approaches to reliability and security.</li><li><strong>Cloud and container experience</strong>, with an understanding of how to deploy, operate, and scale production workloads.</li><li><strong>Fluent English (C1+)</strong>, both written and spoken. </li></ul>Nice to have<ul><li>Experience building <strong>workflow, reporting, questionnaire, or other complex B2B SaaS products</strong>.</li><li>Familiarity with backend technologies such as <strong>FastAPI, PostgreSQL, background queues </strong></li><li>Any experience with <strong><strong>LangChain, LangSmith, or other LLM frameworks</strong></strong></li><li>Deeper experience with <strong>RAG, retrieval, agents, LLM evaluation, and production AI systems</strong>.</li><li>Experience improving <strong>latency, cost, and reliability</strong> for AI workloads.</li><li>Knowledge of <strong>ESG, sustainability, climate tech, or corporate reporting</strong>.</li><li>German language skills.</li></ul>Who you are<ul><li><strong>Kind and collaborative</strong>: You treat people well, communicate clearly, and help create a supportive, low-ego team environment.</li><li><strong>Mission-driven</strong>: You care about using technology to accelerate sustainability and climate action.</li><li><strong>Sharp and curious</strong>: You learn quickly, ask good questions, and enjoy getting to the root of difficult product and technical problems.</li><li><strong>A product-minded builder</strong>: You think beyond the task in front of you, focus on the user’s real problem, and care about whether what you ship creates value.</li><li><strong>Highly self-directed</strong>: You thrive in a fast-moving environment with autonomy, ambiguity, and limited oversight.</li><li><strong>Pragmatic and action-oriented</strong>: You can move from ideas to experiments to production without waiting for perfect requirements.</li><li><strong>Opinionated but open-minded</strong>: You challenge ideas constructively, welcome pushback, and enjoy thinking through problems with others.</li><li><strong>Commercially aware and creative</strong>: You balance technical quality with user needs, business value, and speed.</li></ul>If your experience doesn’t align precisely with all the criteria, don't worry! We encourage you to still apply. Many people miss out on opportunities because they feel they don’t fit every requirement—we believe in attitude, growth and iteration, not perfection!</p><br><strong>What we offer</strong><p><ul><li><strong>Competitive salary and equity</strong>, reflecting your impact and ownership.</li><li><strong>Purpose-driven mission</strong>: Build tools that help organisations act more sustainably and make the ESG data ecosystem more transparent.</li><li><strong>Flexible hybrid setup</strong>: Berlin or London based candidates are strongly preferred, with access to our team and the wider startup community at the Merantix AI Campus.</li><li><strong>Trust and autonomy</strong>: Own meaningful problems, shape the product, and influence how we build as the company grows.</li><li><strong>A genuinely high-impact role</strong>: Increase our delivery capacity, strengthen the robustness of our platform, and accelerate product innovation.</li><li><strong>Dynamic environment</strong>: Work in a small, ambitious team at the intersection of applied AI, enterprise software, and sustainability.</li><li><strong>Learning budget and quarterly hackathons</strong>: Explore new technologies and prototype ideas that push Briink forward.</li><li><strong>A thoughtful hiring process</strong>: We are focused on finding the right person, and are willing to take the time needed to do so.</li></ul></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/merantix/product-engineer-backend-ai-at-briink-berlin-497158","tags":["backend","AI","LLM","product","product engineer","backend engineer","AI engineer"],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1790798947},{"slug":"ai-research-engineer-kernel-inference-optimization-germany-474080","company_name":"Jobgether","title":"AI Research Engineer (Kernel & Inference Optimization)","description":"<div>
<p><strong>This position is listed on behalf of a partner company, who manages all applications and next steps. Our partner is looking for an AI Research Engineer (Kernel &amp; Inference Optimization) based in Germany.</strong></p>
<p>You will work at the intersection of AI research, systems engineering, and high-performance model inference.<br>Your focus will be on developing and optimizing model-serving architectures for advanced AI systems across a range of hardware environments.<br>You will tackle challenges involving latency, throughput, memory efficiency, and scalability, including deployment on resource-constrained mobile and edge devices.<br>The role combines hands-on research with low-level engineering, giving you the opportunity to develop novel inference strategies and GPU kernels.<br>You will work with complex architectures spanning text, image, audio, diffusion models, and vision transformers.<br>Your work will involve rigorous benchmarking, production testing, and iterative optimization to translate research into measurable performance improvements.<br>You will collaborate with cross-functional teams in a highly technical, remote environment focused on pushing the boundaries of efficient AI systems.</p>
</div><br><strong>Accountabilities</strong><br><div>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>Design and deploy advanced model-serving architectures optimized for high throughput, low latency, and efficient memory utilization.</li>
<li>Develop inference pipelines capable of operating effectively across diverse environments, including resource-constrained mobile devices and edge platforms.</li>
<li>Establish clear performance targets covering response latency, token generation speed, throughput, memory footprint, and reliability.</li>
<li>Build and execute controlled inference benchmarks in simulated and production environments, tracking latency, throughput, memory consumption, and error rates.</li>
<li>Create and maintain representative datasets and simulation scenarios for evaluating model performance under real-world and resource-constrained conditions.</li>
<li>Identify computational and memory bottlenecks across inference pipelines and implement solutions involving batching, networking, memory management, and other system-level optimizations.</li>
<li>Develop custom GPU kernels and compute shaders for mobile hardware, including solutions written in Metal Shading Language (MSL).</li>
<li>Apply advanced inference optimization techniques such as pruning, quantization, Flash Attention, KV caching, and speculative decoding.</li>
<li>Design and optimize distributed inference systems using approaches such as tensor parallelism, pipeline parallelism, and expert parallelism for large-scale GPU workloads.</li>
<li>Work with cross-functional engineering and research teams to integrate optimized inference frameworks into production and edge-device applications.</li>
<li>Define evaluation methodologies, document experimental results, compare performance against established benchmarks, and continuously refine optimization strategies.</li>
<li>Monitor production performance and use empirical research to identify opportunities for further improvements in scalability, efficiency, and reliability.</li>

<h3>Requirements:</h3>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>Degree in Computer Science or a related technical field; a PhD in NLP, Machine Learning, or a related discipline is highly relevant, particularly with a strong AI research track record and publications at leading conferences.</li>
<li>Proven expertise in Metal Shading Language (MSL), including the ability to write custom compute shaders from scratch.</li>
<li>Demonstrated experience with low-level kernel optimization and inference optimization on mobile or other resource-constrained devices.</li>
<li>Track record of delivering measurable improvements in inference latency, throughput, and memory footprint for domain-specific applications.</li>
<li>Deep understanding of modern model-serving architectures, inference engines, and optimization techniques for high-performance AI deployment.</li>
<li>Strong experience writing GPU kernels for mobile devices such as smartphones.</li>
<li>Practical experience developing and deploying end-to-end inference pipelines, from model optimization through production integration on constrained hardware.</li>
<li>Strong ability to apply empirical research and systematic experimentation to solve latency, computational, and memory challenges.</li>
<li>Experience designing robust evaluation and benchmarking frameworks for inference systems.</li>
<li>Knowledge of distributed inference techniques, including tensor parallelism, pipeline parallelism, and expert parallelism for large-scale GPU clusters.</li>
<li>Deep understanding of the mathematical foundations and architecture of diffusion models and Vision Transformers.</li>
<li>Familiarity with modern inference optimization techniques including pruning, quantization, Flash Attention, KV Cache optimization, and speculative decoding such as EAGLE.</li>
<li>Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities, with an ability to investigate complex system bottlenecks and turn research findings into practical engineering solutions.</li>
<li>Excellent English communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with distributed, cross-functional technical teams.</li>

<h3>Benefits:</h3>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>Opportunity to work on advanced AI systems spanning model serving, inference optimization, mobile computing, edge deployment, and large-scale distributed inference.</li>
<li>Remote-first working environment with an international team.</li>
<li>Exposure to cutting-edge AI research and practical systems engineering challenges.</li>
<li>Opportunity to contribute to performance-critical infrastructure where improvements can have a measurable impact on real-world AI applications.</li>
<li>Collaborative environment combining research-driven experimentation with hands-on engineering.</li>
<li>Opportunity to work with advanced model architectures including diffusion models, Vision Transformers, and multimodal systems.</li>
