ialisés pour explorer en parallèle les codes, jurisprudences, doctrines et textes européens. Chaque source est minutieusement analysée, les liens implicites entre principes sont identifiés, et toutes les informations sont synthétisées dans un rapport structuré, avec chaque affirmation soigneusement sourcée. Ce qui, auparavant, demandait une semaine à une équipe se réalise désormais pendant une pause café.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notre mission : rendre le droit plus rapide, plus clair et plus fiable, afin que les avocats et les directions juridiques puissent se concentrer sur l'essentiel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nous construisons l'équipe commerciale en France, et nous cherchons la personne qui va structurer et faire grandir l'équipe d'Account Executives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pourquoi rejoindre Lexroom ?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Un produit qui tient ses promesses : nos démos sont impactantes et convainquent dès la première session, pas besoin de six mois de POC.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Un marché en pleine effervescence : tous les cabinets français recherchent une solution IA, et les usages sont encore à inventer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Un avantage concurrentiel fort : vous ne vendez pas un assistant IA de plus, mais une approche radicalement nouvelle que les prospects n'ont jamais vue.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Un vrai rôle de bâtisseur : vous définissez les standards, les process et la culture commerciale de l'équipe dès le départ.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vos responsabilités</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Piloter le revenu outbound SMB : objectifs d'ARR, couverture de pipeline, taux de conversion, durée de cycle, ACV, gestion rigoureuse des remises, prévisions fiables.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manager et coacher une équipe d'AE full-cycle : 1:1 hebdomadaires, revues de pipeline, coaching sur les appels, stratégie de deals, plans d'amélioration concrets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Construire la machine outbound : segmentation ICP, découpage des territoires, stratégie de sourcing des comptes, prospection multicanale (téléphone, email, LinkedIn), standards de cadence et suivi activité → résultats.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruter, onboarder et faire monter en compétence les AE, avec un plan de ramp-up et des jalons clairs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gérer la performance : attentes claires, rituels hebdomadaires (WBR), diagnostic des causes (compétence, motivation, territoire, message) et action rapide en cas de sous-performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborer avec le Marketing (campagnes, contenus, événements), les Partenariats (canaux locaux, KOLs) et le Produit (remontée des insights terrain).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Garantir la discipline process et outils : CRM irréprochable, séquences rigoureuses, reporting fiable. Les faits avant les impressions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Profil recherché</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expérience confirmée en management commercial outbound SMB dans le SaaS B2B, avec une équipe d'AE full-cycle atteignant régulièrement ses objectifs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expertise terrain : vous savez vous-même lancer des séquences, faire du cold call et enseigner une prospection qui convertit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mindset de coach : vous identifiez rapidement les écarts de performance et coachez de façon structurée (écoute d'appels, scorecards), pas avec des discours de motivation génériques.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Profil data-driven : à l'aise avec la funnel math (activité → meetings → démos → essais → closing), le forecast et la couverture de pipeline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maîtrise des outils : CRM (HubSpot/Salesforce), outils de séquençage et d'automatisation, Sales Navigator, et une vraie exigence sur la qualité des données.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Français natif, anglais courant (clientèle francophone, équipes internes internationales).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intérêt pour le droit : une expérience dans le secteur juridique ou des services professionnels est un plus, mais pas indispensable.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ce que nous offrons</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rémunération fixe: 70 000 € + bonus sur performance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mutuelle Alan, titres-restaurant, accès Wellpass (sport et bien-être)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travail hybride, bureaux à Paris</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team retreats et off-sites</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Processus de recrutement</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entretien Talent Acquisition : motivation et parcours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entretien avec le hiring manager : expérience de management et approche commerciale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business case : construction d'un plan outbound et gestion d'une situation de performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entretien final : valeurs et culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offre.</p></li></ol><hr><p>Compensation: €70K – €110K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • €70K – €110K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lexroom/account-executive-manager-smb-french-market-paris-259275","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1790797209},{"slug":"senior-solution-engineer-fr-france-205908","company_name":"Filigran","title":"Senior Solution Engineer (FR)","description":"<h2>🌀 The Company</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founded in 2022, Filigran is a global cybersecurity company on a mission to empower defense teams to be proactive through open-source solutions that uncover threats and drive action.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Filigran stands out in the cybersecurity ecosystem through its open-source, AI-powered and threat-informed approach to Continuous Threat Exposure Management (CTEM). Our eXtended Threat Management (XTM) platform brings together threat intelligence, exposure validation and cyber risk reduction, enabling organizations to better understand their threat landscape and take action.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of Filigran is our open-source approach. Our vision is to unite defenders into a global community to make security more open, resilient and collaborative.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Filigran continues to scale globally, we are building the organization, infrastructure and capabilities needed for our next stage of growth. How we scale matters just as much as how fast we scale: our CORE values: Cohesion, Openness, Responsibility and Equity  shape how we work together, make decisions and build for the future.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>🎯 The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a <strong>Senior Solution Engineer</strong> to join our <strong>Go-to-Market team</strong> and help us guide our most strategic prospects and customers in adopting and integrating Filigran’s open source platforms — OpenCTI &amp; OpenAEV. You’ll play a key role at the intersection of technical expertise and client enablement by running demos, delivering workshops, building prototypes, and translating customer needs into integrated technical solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work will directly support our Sales, Customer Success, and Product teams by enabling strong adoption, trust, and long-term success with Filigran’s ecosystem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>💼 Your Responsibilities</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver technical and functional guidance to key prospects and customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and run product demonstrations and workshops tailored to use cases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design technical solutions aligned to customer architecture and business goals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead successful Proof-of-Value (PoV) deployments and maintain healthy environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support smooth handovers from Sales to Customer Success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Filigran as a technical advisor in client discussions, from dev teams to C-level</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to technical documentation, training, and integration projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain strong relationships with the OpenCTI community and users</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Product, Engineering, and Marketing to feed back insights and influence the roadmap</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🤝 Who You’ll Work With</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reports to the CRO or Head of Presales (depending on region)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Works cross-functionally with Sales, Customer Success, Product, and Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborates closely with leadership (CEO, CRO) on go-to-market strategies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engages with community members and technical users of our open source platforms</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🧬 Profile We’re Looking For</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in a Solution Engineering, Technical Account Management, Consulting, or Presales role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of cybersecurity or crisis management topics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to explain technical concepts to both engineering and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading workshops, technical trainings, or product demos</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable operating in a remote-first, fast-paced, and collaborative environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in French and English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus: Prior experience in threat intelligence, SOC, breach and attack simulation/pentesting or public sector cybersecurity</p></li></ul><h2>🌱 <strong>Why Join Filigran? More than just a job.</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a <strong>fast-growing, global and remote-first company</strong>, and we believe the best work combines <strong>purpose, impact and innovation</strong>. You’ll work alongside talented people across the world who care about what they build, how they build it, and the impact they make on the broader cybersecurity ecosystem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">⭐ <strong>Be part of something bigger</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe we do work that matters. Our open-source approach means that work extends beyond Filigran. You’re contributing to technology and ideas that strengthen a global community of defenders and help make cybersecurity more open and collaborative.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 <strong>Work at the edge of what’s next</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We bring together cybersecurity, open source and AI — giving you the opportunity to work with emerging technologies, experiment with new ways of working, and contribute to how they are applied in practice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 <strong>Global opportunity without borders</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of a fast-growing, truly international team — collaborating across Europe, North America, APJ and beyond, with the flexibility of a remote-first environment. As we grow, you’ll have opportunities to expand your scope, take ownership, learn quickly and grow with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧭 <strong>A culture grounded in CORE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cohesion, Openness, Responsibility and Equity</strong> define how we work together — with openness, ownership, collaboration and respect. These are the principles that guide how we make decisions, treat people and grow together, especially when no one’s watching.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>💰 <strong>What you can expect</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation + equity</strong> — everyone shares in our success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first flexibility</strong> — work from wherever you’re based, with flexibility built into how we operate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>25 days PTO baseline</strong> — real time to disconnect, recharge and enjoy life outside work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Volunteer days</strong> — paid time to contribute to causes that matter to you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set up for success</strong> — choose the equipment that works for you, with additional support for your remote work and development needs as our programs evolve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Two annual in-person get-togethers</strong> — one global company get-together and one team get-together, creating dedicated time to connect, collaborate and strengthen our culture beyond the screen</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>🌍 <strong>Equal Employment Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We enable cybersecurity through inclusion — from code to culture.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Filigran, we are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We believe the diversity of our people makes our products and our team stronger. We welcome talent of every background, identity and lived experience, regardless of race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or veteran status.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What matters here is what you bring, not what you look like, where you’re from or how you identify.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🚀 <strong>Ready to Join Us?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply now and help us build the future of the cybersecurity ecosystem, together.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/filigran/senior-solution-engineer-fr-france-205908","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"France","created_at":1790797207},{"slug":"accounting-manager-paris-277675","company_name":"Aninebing","title":"Accounting Manager","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt; is looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Accounting Manager &lt;/strong&gt;to join our Finance team based in Paris.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is an opportunity to help shape the next chapter of ANINE BING. As a key contributor within our Paris HQ team, the Accounting Manager brings both strategic insight and hands-on execution to their work — supporting our global growth while staying grounded in the brand&#39;s DNA: refined, fast-moving, and always evolving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a senior, hands-on accounting professional who thrives in a creative yet performance-driven environment. The ideal candidate combines strong technical accounting expertise with a project management mindset, a genuine sensitivity to Finance × IT topics (AP automation, ERP improvements), and a structured, team-oriented approach. They are rigorous, organized, and energized by leading a team and building scalable accounting processes across an international footprint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Global Accounting Director, the Accounting Manager owns the day-to-day accounts payable and general accounting operations across our directly-managed entities — France, the UK, the US and other EU markets. The role manages a team of three (AP Accountant, General Accountant, and Intern) and acts as the operational anchor of the accounting team, ensuring clean books, timely closes and strong vendor relationships. The role is expected to operate as a true business partner to all operational departments, not as a back-office function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid position based at our Paris HQ, with one remote day per week (Wednesday or Friday). The role reports to the Accounting &amp;amp; Tax Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities Include:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end accounts payable process across all directly-managed entities: vendor onboarding, invoice processing, payment runs, expense reports, and vendor relationship management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the general accounting operations: journal entries, bank reconciliations, fixed assets, accruals, prepayments, and intercompany bookings — ensuring accurate, timely month-end and year-end closes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop a team of three (AP Accountant, General Accountant, Intern): set priorities, coach, review work and build technical depth within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Accounting &amp;amp; Tax Director on the design and implementation of accounting policies, internal controls and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Finance × IT initiatives within scope: AP automation tools, ERP improvements, expense management systems and approval workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support statutory audits and tax filings by preparing required schedules, reconciliations and supporting documentation across entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a true business partner to Operations, Procurement, Retail and HQ teams — building trust, anticipating needs and ensuring smooth vendor management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive experience in accounting, including at least 2 years managing a team of accountants in an international, multi-entity environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior profile with a strong hands-on mindset: comfortable balancing managerial responsibilities with direct, detailed accounting work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical command of French GAAP; exposure to US GAAP or IFRS is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid hands-on expertise across AP and general accounting: full close cycle, reconciliations, intercompany, accruals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven project management mindset and Finance × IT sensitivity: experience leading process and system improvements (ERP rollouts, AP automation, expense management tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine business partner mindset, with the ability to engage and collaborate effectively with all operational departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven people management skills — including hiring, coaching, and developing junior accountants and interns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English required; French is a strong asset. Comfortable operating across time zones, including with US-based teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in retail, fashion, e-commerce or consumer goods is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HQ FRANCE: &lt;/strong&gt;At ANINE BING Paris, we combine creative ambition with a people-first culture. Expect generous time off (including RTT), a hybrid schedule with one remote day per week, exclusive discounts on our collections, and private sales access — so you can live the brand as much as you build it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Style Perks: &lt;/strong&gt;Enjoy a generous employee discount and seasonal wardrobe allotments — so you can live the brand, not just represent it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Bonus: &lt;/strong&gt;Eligibility for an annual performance bonus of 10% of base salary, tied to close quality, process improvements and team development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The target gross annual base salary for this role is between €70,000 and €85,000, depending on experience, with eligibility for an annual performance bonus of 10%.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Working at ANINE BING&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING seeks to empower its employees by providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants and teammates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, Veteran status, or other legally protected characteristics. Diversity and inclusion is critical to our success as a global brand, and we seek to recruit, develop, and retain the most talented people from a diverse candidate pool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;More about ANINE BING&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is a Los Angeles-based fashion house founded in 2012 that blends elements of Scandinavian simplicity with American energy to offer modern wardrobe essentials for women seeking a timeless yet rebellious approach to everyday style. Since its launch, ANINE BING has evolved into a global brand, available in over 90 countries with a growing network of brick-and-mortar retail stores in key cities worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Powered by a global team of over 250 employees, ANINE BING is headquartered in Los Angeles and Paris, with additional offices in New York and Shanghai.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Our Paris HQ&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Located just off the Champs-Élysées, our Paris headquarters at 1 Rue François 1er is a cornerstone of our international growth. As the home of our Product teams and other key functions, this space reflects our commitment to creativity, collaboration, and global perspective. As we continue to grow across Europe, our Paris office plays a central role in shaping the future of our brand.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/aninebing/accounting-manager-paris-277675","tags":["Finance & Accounting"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1790787368},{"slug":"staff-product-manager-decathlon-app-permanent-cdi-paris-paris-56755","company_name":"Decathlontechnology","title":"Staff Product Manager – Decathlon App [Permanent - CDI] (f/m/d)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notre équipe Decathlon App recherche un·e Staff Product Manager (f/m/d) en CDI basé·e à Lille ou Paris.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cœur de l&#39;écosystème digital de Decathlon, l&#39;équipe &lt;strong&gt;Decathlon App&lt;/strong&gt; fait le pont entre nos expériences e-commerce et le commerce physique. Notre mission dépasse la simple transaction : nous construisons un compagnon sportif quotidien, personnalisé et enrichi pour accompagner des millions d&#39;utilisateur·ices dans leur pratique. Rejoindre notre équipe produit globale (iOS &amp;amp; Android), c&#39;est évoluer dans un environnement stimulant où l&#39;autonomie, l&#39;impact à grande échelle et l&#39;excellence méthodologique sont au cœur de nos défis quotidiens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que Staff Product Manager (f/m/d), tu apporteras la vision stratégique et l&#39;architecture fonctionnelle nécessaires pour faire passer notre application mobile à l&#39;échelle supérieure. Tu opéreras avec une grande autonomie sur des enjeux complexes pour transformer l&#39;expérience Decathlon App et garantir la cohérence de l&#39;écosystème.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tes responsabilités s&#39;articulent autour de 4 piliers stratégiques :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignement stratégique, gestion des parties prenantes &amp;amp; vision app&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter la valeur globale (&lt;em&gt;macro view&lt;/em&gt;) générée par les initiatives mobiles clés sur l&#39;ensemble de l&#39;écosystème business et client, au-delà des backlogs d&#39;équipes individuelles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Porter la vision produit auprès de la direction exécutive, des leaders business et des parties prenantes transversales pour aligner l&#39;organisation sur la roadmap de l&#39;application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Définir les orientations stratégiques sur les segments utilisateurs prioritaires sur les points de contact mobiles natifs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suivre et optimiser les métriques de performance macro tout au long du funnel : notoriété, trafic, conversion, rétention et taux de réachat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture fonctionnelle &amp;amp; orchestration End-to-End&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agir en tant qu&#39;Architecte Fonctionnel·le principal·e en définissant la répartition des périmètres entre les squads afin d&#39;éliminer les frictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travailler en triade étroite avec les Staff Tech/Principal Engineers et les Staff UX Designers pour aligner l&#39;architecture technique, les systèmes de design et la vision produit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concevoir des parcours omnicanaux sans couture reliant la découverte mobile, les interactions en magasin (ex: Scan &amp;amp; Go, retrait), le paiement et les services sportifs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sparring stratégique &amp;amp; de-risking produit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conseiller et accompagner les Group Product Managers (GPM) et Product Managers (PM) face aux dépendances complexes de l&#39;application et aux pièges classiques du produit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structurer des stratégies de réduction des risques (&lt;em&gt;de-risking&lt;/em&gt;) sur les projets majeurs pour identifier au plus tôt les enjeux d&#39;appétence, de viabilité et d&#39;utilisabilité.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mener des boucles de validation concrètes (A/B testing, multivariés, tests d&#39;utilisabilité de prototypes) pour valider les hypothèses avant le déploiement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Élévation de la culture &amp;amp; des pratiques produit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accompagner la communauté PM vers les meilleures pratiques produit modernes (frameworks de discovery, expérimentation continue, Opportunity Solution Trees - OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promouvoir l&#39;adoption des possibilités liées à l&#39;IA et des méthodologies avancées pour enrichir l&#39;expérience utilisateur et l&#39;efficacité des squads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Jouer un rôle de multiplicateur d&#39;impact pour faire grandir la communauté Produit, sans agir en tant que manager hiérarchique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE TU APPORTES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
